\DOC MEMSAFE_BITVAL_TAC

\TYPE {MEMSAFE_BITVAL_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Prefixes the goal's conclusion with implication antecedents bounding by 1 each
distinct {bitval}-headed subterm of the conclusion, leaving the conclusion
unchanged when there are none.

\DESCRIBE
Takes no arguments. The conclusion is scanned for subterms of the form
{bitval u}, and one antecedent is added per distinct such subterm, in an
unspecified order (not the order of occurrence); when n is zero the goal is
returned unchanged.
{
          A ?- t
   ================================  MEMSAFE_BITVAL_TAC
     A ?- bitval u1 <= 1 ==> ... ==> bitval un <= 1 ==> t
}

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this single kind of transformation, on goals
whose conclusions are arithmetic inequalities over natural numbers, either
containing several {bitval} applications or none at all.

\ENDDOC
